So rule: output cell = 3 if leftcell == rightcell == primary_right; else = primary_right. Where primary_right = the right-side color that... which is primary? In demo2 right colors {7,4}: 7 is primary (more frequent? 7 count vs 4 count: 7s many). In demo1 right {8,5}: 8 primary. So primary = most frequent right color? demo2: count 4s: rows list: r0:0,r1:2,r2:1,r3:3,r4:2,r5:1,r6:2,r7:1,r8:0,r9:3,r10:1,r11:2,r12:1,r13:2,r14:0,r15:2,r16:2,r17:0,r18:0,r19:1 = 26. 7s = 120-26... total cells 20*6=120, so 7s=94. Yes 7 dominant. Demo1 right {8,5}: 8s: row0 5, row1 4, row2 5 =14; 5s = 33-14=19! Wait 3*11=33 cells. 5s: row0 {3,4,5,6,8,9}=6, row1 {0,1,2,3,4,5,8,10}=8, row2 {1,3,4,5,7,9}=6 → 20; 8s = 13. So 5 is more frequent than 8 in demo1! So primary ≠ most frequent. Hmm.

